    <string name="spatial_switch">Spatial audio</string>
    <string name="spatial_caption">Experimental; the author could not hear a difference. Some vivo models (TWS Air 3 Pro) only. ⚠️ Take the earbuds out and set volume to minimum before toggling: sudden loud noise can damage hearing.</string>
    <string name="spatial_toast">Experimental: take the earbuds out first</string>
    <string name="spatial_dialog_title">Experimental feature</string>
    <string name="spatial_dialog_msg">This switch is experimental. The vivo TWS Air3 Pro reports its switch state. The audible effect still needs testing.\n\n⚠️ Toggling may cause sudden volume changes or loud noise. Take the earbuds out and set the volume to minimum. Put them back on when it is safe.\n\nContinue?</string>
    <string name="deepx_label">DeepX audio</string>
    <string name="equalizer_label">Built-in EQ</string>
    <string name="deepx_caption">May take a few seconds to apply. Some vivo models (TWS Air 3 Pro) only. Take the earbuds out and lower the volume while testing; do not switch repeatedly.</string>
    <string name="dialog_ok">I understand, continue</string>
    <string name="dialog_cancel">Cancel</string>
    <string name="global_disclaimer_title">Disclaimer</string>
    <string name="global_disclaimer_msg">This is an unofficial, unauthorized third-party research tool that controls the earbuds by reverse-engineered private protocol. It collects and uploads no data.\nGitHub: https://github.com/hdzw1155/WearEars\n\n⚠️ Safety: private commands are not certified by the vendor. They may cause sudden loud noise, feedback or volume jumps and damage your hearing. Before connecting a new model, the first use after a firmware update, or before enabling any feature marked "EXP", take the earbuds out (do not wear them), set volume to minimum, and only put them on after confirming it is safe. Do not use while driving, cycling or operating machinery.\n\nHearing damage is irreversible. Please be careful. You use this app entirely at your own risk.\n\nDo you agree and want to continue?</string>
    <string name="disclaimer_page_msg">This is an unofficial, unauthorized third-party research tool that controls the earbuds by reverse-engineered private protocol. It collects and uploads no data.\nGitHub: https://github.com/hdzw1155/WearEars\n\n⚠️ Safety: private commands are not certified by the vendor. They may cause sudden loud noise, feedback or volume jumps and damage your hearing. Before connecting a new model, the first use after a firmware update, or before enabling any feature marked "EXP", take the earbuds out (do not wear them), set volume to minimum, and only put them on after confirming it is safe. Do not use while driving, cycling or operating machinery.\n\nHearing damage is irreversible. Please be careful. You use this app entirely at your own risk.</string>
    <string name="dialog_agree">I understand and agree</string>
    <string name="dialog_refuse">Disagree and exit</string>
    <string name="disclaimer">Disclaimer: a personal research project, not affiliated with vivo / Huawei / Xiaomi / Edifier / Samsung / Qualcomm. "Developer" holds experimental commands inferred from reverse engineering and validated on some models (e.g. vivo TWS Air 3 Pro).\nGitHub: https://github.com/hdzw1155/WearEars\n⚠️ Before any experimental toggle: take the earbuds out, set volume to minimum, then wear them after confirming it is safe. Hearing damage is irreversible. Do not use while driving or cycling.\nYou use this app entirely at your own risk, including but not limited to hearing discomfort, property loss, firmware issues, data loss or security risks.</string>

